MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes all 4 blockers the audit found against ROADMAP §5.

Safety
- gate every Write button, not just Write all (per-tab writes went to the
  wire with no confirm and no backup check)
- computeDelta: show which values change before the frame leaves
- AutoDetect: infer motor family from the GEN current ceiling and clamp to
  18/25/30A; block a write that exceeds it
- ACK watchdog: 2500ms deadline, loud failure instead of a frozen UI

Protocol
- verifyRxChecksum replaces "// checksum ignored"; strict mode discards
  frames that do not verify. Response checksum span still needs confirming
  on real hardware — logged both candidates for that purpose.

Reality Check
- drop REF_MAX_KMH=45; speed ceiling now comes from gearing x crank RPM x
  rolling circumference. Reference rig 32T/11T/27.5x2.8 -> 47.8 km/h
- wheel diameter from ETRTO rim + tire width instead of nominal inches
- thermal heuristic: >=22A AND cadence <60rpm, plus which cog to shift to
- Crr/CdA become surface and position presets
- drop CONTROLLER_MAX_A=25; gauges scale to the real hardware

UI
- delta list paints a current/heat rise red, never green
- honour prefers-reduced-motion
- remove sessionStorage (project bans Web Storage)

Tools
- tools/Audit-BbsFlash.ps1 (PowerShell 7) - DoD audit, exit code = blockers
- tools/smoke.mjs - headless Chromium, 18 assertions

